  "description": "BALLISTIC CARBON LAYUP\n\nThe iLynx Trail Carbon are made of carbon, using the HCIM (Hollow Core Internal Moulding) carbon moulding technology that allows the weight of the frame and tie rod to be reduced to a minimum. It has been made using “Ballistic Carbon Layup” carbon fibres, which offer outstanding impact resistance. So the frame weighs just 1,975 g.\n\nBH2EXMAG. GEN 2\n\nimproving the user experience. New telemetry torque sensor, provides 3 times the assistance gradually and very quietly.\n\nADDITIONAL XPRO BATTERY, PLUG & RIDE\n\nAll models come equipped with a 630Wh battery located in the down tube, weighing 2.6 kg. This battery, composed of 21700 cells with 5.8Ah, offers maximum energy density and allows more energy to be stored in a compact space, resulting in a low center of gravity for natural handling. Additionally, the external XPro battery provides an extra 180Wh, increasing the range to 4600m of elevation gain.\n\n150MM\n\nThe iLynx Trail offers 150 mm of travel, with a Split Pivot suspension system allowing you to ride on any terrain. Maintaining 100% anti-squat - ensuring pedalling efficiency - and brake squat - ensuring outstanding braking.\n\nOVERSIZED MAIN SUSPENSION AXLE\n\nThe iLynx Trail frame provides maximum stiffness thanks to the main suspension axle being oversized, thus optimising the stiffness of the front and rear triangles and increasing torsional stiffness. Its geometry is very similar to the standard BH Lynx Trail, with the rear measuring only 451mm, enabling dynamic riding and notably improving handling during descents.\n\nSUPERBOOST 157 X 12\n\nThe new Super Boost increases the strength and resistance of the rear wheel thanks to better “truing” or tension on both sides of the wheel. This is combined with short chainstays that significantly improve manoeuvrability on descents and a large tyre width clearance for wider tyres measuring up to 2.4”.",
